1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,780
The next question is from NYX22.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:06,900
Mr. Avila, are you scared for your life and is Brazil protecting you?

3
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:09,640
Thank you for bringing that up, NYX22.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,860
We always discuss this on the boat, Amanda,

5
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:16,520
that people were discussing when we were like two days before interception.

6
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:18,660
And people were saying, are you scared to everyone?

7
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:22,980
And most of the people would say, no, I'm more scared of not fulfilling our mission,

8
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,460
of living our life in vain, of the future that my daughter will live at.

9
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:32,000
So I'm much more concerned for the future generations than for anyone's life.

10
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,900
We need to do this. It's our historical duty to do so.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,700
So we have a very serious risk assessment.

12
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,800
I train our participants in nonviolence direct action

13
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:44,780
and how they need to behave in case of an interception, for example,

14
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,340
to escalate stuff.

15
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:50,220
So we take this very, very seriously, but we do not stop for that.

16
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:52,620
Otherwise, what would be the history of humanity

17
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:55,480
if people would stop doing something important because it's dangerous?

18
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:58,560
So we need to understand this danger, work with it,

19
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,120
and try to neutralize as many dangers as we can

20
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:06,600
and try to reduce the impact of the damage that we cannot neutralize and continue.

21
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:09,300
And Brazil is not protecting me at all.

22
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,980
Actually, Brazil didn't break relations with Israel,

23
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,900
despite the fact that they kidnapped the Brazilian system.

24
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,820
We get it. We understand what you're saying.

25
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:16,700
Putting on solitary confinement.

26
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:17,880
That was very diplomatic.

27
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:22,180
But Brazil is an ally of the Palestinian cause

28
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:24,200
and it still has contradictions,

29
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:25,880
but at least on speech,

30
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:29,220
President Lula gives very good speeches denouncing the genocide.

31
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:31,940
We get it.

32
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:33,500
We understand what you're saying.

33
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:35,400
That was very diplomatic.

34
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:40,800
Amen.

35
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:40,840
Amen.

36
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,140
Amen.

